1
00:00:11,790 --> 00:00:18,790
If there is a spill inside the BSC, it must be cleaned and decontaminated promptly.

2
00:00:18,790 --> 00:00:22,790
Wearing appropriate PPE is crucial for this.

3
00:00:22,790 --> 00:00:29,790
Standard operating procedures, or SOPs, should be developed in advance for how to respond to spills.

4
00:00:29,790 --> 00:00:36,790
Cleanup of large spills, or spills that occur in parts of the BSC that are difficult to access,

5
00:00:36,790 --> 00:00:43,790
for example the drained spillage trough or catch basin, may require assistance from the safety office.

6
00:00:43,790 --> 00:00:50,790
The following demonstrates a general procedure for small spills that occur on the work surface.

7
00:00:50,790 --> 00:00:58,790
This procedure may need to be adjusted according to the specific work being performed and your laboratory SOPs.

8
00:00:58,790 --> 00:01:05,790
The first thing you should do is cover the spill with an absorbent material such as paper towels.

9
00:01:05,790 --> 00:01:19,790
Using a plastic squirt bottle, carefully apply the designated liquid disinfectant in your SOP to the absorbent starting at the outside of the spill and moving toward the center in circular motions.

10
00:01:19,790 --> 00:01:28,810
Wipe up as much of the spill as possible and discard the towels in the biohazardous waste container.

11
00:01:29,810 --> 00:01:41,810
Then, repeat the process with more paper towels and disinfectant, this time leaving the wet paper towels on top of the contaminated area for the appropriate contact time to allow for disinfection.

12
00:01:41,810 --> 00:01:54,810
Contact time will vary depending on the organic material and specific infectious agents present, the type and concentration of the disinfectant, the concentration of the agent and other variables.

13
00:01:55,810 --> 00:01:58,810
Discard the paper towels in the biohazardous waste container.

14
00:01:58,810 --> 00:02:11,940
If bleach was used, swipe the surface with ethanol or water to remove the residual bleach and prevent pitting of the stainless steel.

15
00:02:11,940 --> 00:02:24,420
If objects inside the BSC came in contact with the spill, they must also be decontaminated.

16
00:02:24,420 --> 00:02:30,420
Apply disinfectant to paper towels and wipe the exterior surfaces.

17
00:02:30,420 --> 00:02:36,420
Make sure the objects are wetted for the proper contact time before resuming work.
